React conventions for this repo. Pairs with `typescript.mdc` (language hygiene) and `map.mdc` (SVG town map). Keep this file to rules that are not obvious from `package.json`, `tsconfig*.json`, or framework defaults.

## Stack

- **Build**: Vite 5 + `@vitejs/plugin-react`, TypeScript strict mode.
- **UI**: React + inline SVG for the town map. See `map.mdc`.
- **Styling**: CSS Modules + CSS variables. No Tailwind, no CSS-in-JS.
- **State**: local `useState` lifted to `App.tsx`; the active locale's content flows through `ContentContext`. There is no router, store, or server state; do not add Zustand/React Query/React Router unless the feature genuinely needs it.

## Folder Layout

```
src/
├── main.tsx            # React root only
├── App.tsx             # Owns `active` section (URL hash) and locale, mounts <TownMap> + DOM UI
├── index.css           # Global reset + CSS design tokens (:root)
├── components/         # DOM (HTML) UI rendered outside the canvas
├── content/            # All user-visible text and portfolio data
├── configs/            # Tunable numbers/colors: map views, SVG palette
├── hooks/              # Shared React hooks
├── types/              # Shared types and enums
└── utils/              # Pure helpers (create when first needed)
```

- Never put user-visible strings in components; add them to both `src/content/vi/` and `src/content/en/` (`copy.ts` for fixed UI text, the other files for portfolio data) and read them with `useContent()`. Locale-independent data (`contact.ts`, `SECTION_IDS`) stays at the `src/content/` root.
- Never hardcode tunable numbers that other files depend on (map positions, zoom levels, colors) inside components; put them in `src/configs/`.

## Path Aliases

- Always import across folders with the `@/` alias (`@/content`, `@/configs`). Relative imports are only for files in the same component directory (`./index.module.css`, `./AboutContent`).
- Never use `../`.

## Files And Exports

- Every public component is a PascalCase directory with `index.tsx` (`TopBar/index.tsx`). Private sub-components are PascalCase files in the same directory (`Panel/AboutContent.tsx`) and are not re-exported.
- Hooks, configs, content, types, utils: camelCase filenames (`hooks/keyboard.ts`, `configs/mapViews.ts`).
- Components use a default export. Everything else uses named exports.
- Every folder of shared modules has a barrel: `components/index.tsx`, `content/index.ts`, `configs/index.ts`, `hooks/index.ts`, `types/index.ts`. Component barrels use `export { default as Name } from './Name';`; others use `export * from './file';`. Keep barrel lines sorted (enforced by `simple-import-sort/exports`).
- Module-level constants are `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` (`SECTION_VIEWS`, `PALETTE`, `HOVER_SCALE`).

## Types

- Shared types live in `src/types/` (`section.ts`, `content.ts`, `map.ts`). Component props stay in the component file as `interface <Name>Props`.
- Section ids are the `ENUM_SECTION` enum. Any lookup keyed by section must be `Record<ENUM_SECTION, ...>` so TypeScript fails the build when a section is added but one of its pieces is missing (label, map view, panel content).
- Use `Vec2` from `@/types` for map coordinates, not `number[]`.
- Content objects are `readonly`; use `as const` for literal maps.

## Components

- Body order: hooks → derived values → handlers → return.
- Name handlers `handleX` inside the component; name props `onX`.
- Boolean props start with `is`/`has`/`can` (`isSmall`).
- Compose conditional classes with `clsx`, never string concatenation.
- Keep components presentational; state lives in `App.tsx` and flows down as `active` / `onSelect` / `onClose`.

## Styling

- Each component that needs styles has `index.module.css` next to its `index.tsx`. Class names are camelCase (`.navButton`, `.brandTitle`).
- Colors, radii and other shared values come from CSS variables in `src/index.css`. Do not hardcode hex colors in modules; add a token instead.
- `index.css` holds only tokens and the global reset. No component styles in global CSS.
- Put responsive (`@media (max-width: 700px)`) and `prefers-reduced-motion` rules in the module that owns the element.
- Avoid inline `style={{}}` except for truly dynamic runtime values.
- DOM colors (`index.css`) and SVG map colors (`configs/palette.ts`) are separate sources; when changing the theme, update both.

## Accessibility

- Every map district must have a DOM equivalent (the nav buttons in `TopBar`), so the site works with keyboard and screen readers.
- Icon-only buttons need an `aria-label` from `COPY`.
- `Escape` closes the open panel (`useKeyDown` in `App.tsx`); keep it working.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for new CSS animations.

## Public Assets

- Static files go under `public/` by purpose: `public/models/` for `.glb`, `public/textures/`, `public/images/`. Lowercase kebab-case filenames.
- Reference them through Vite's base URL, never a bare `/`: `` `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}models/cat.glb` ``. The site may be deployed under a subpath (GitHub Pages `/<repo>/`).
- When renaming or removing an asset, update every reference in the same change.
